{
  "$comment": "Claude's tools, defined once (spec SPECs/opencode-backend-spec.md, A11): tool name -> neutral kind, role, argument names and label words. Read by src-tauri/src/agent/tool_table.rs (include_str!) and features/agent/web/lib/tool-kinds.ts (JSON import); a vectors test on each side pins the rows. The only file besides claude_stream.rs and the Claude adapter that spells a Claude tool name (a boundary test says so). Kinds are the web's: execute, edit, read, search, fetch, agent, other. `role` is what shared code needs beyond the kind: read (one file's content: a role's `read` capability), shell (the shell tool: its window blames file changes, its prefix rules), replace / multi-replace / create (how an edit's input reads: edit_inverse.rs), launch (starts a sub-agent: `agentType` and `background` name its arguments), handback (a sub-agent delivers its report). `args.primary` are the input keys tried, in order, for the one-line label (the web's); `args.paths` are the input keys an edit's file path is read from (Rust's capture); the other args name the input keys of an edit (`old`, `new`, `all`, `edits`, `content`). A row without `past`, `present`, `noun` or `primary` takes the `fallback`'s. `readsFile`: the call opens one file. `protocolOnly` are Claude tool names the protocol knows that have no row (the boundary tests scan for them too). `mcp` classifies Writer's own MCP tools by their name after `prefix`.",
